Same here, so I have created a small workaround python script for that - you can put it into your global opencode directory and it will create a child folder "api_keys" and it will look into opencode.json for all the keys and will then look into the .env file that references them and will create individual files with those mapped keys into the api_keys directory...

I have tried to find which version of opencode introduced this issue, but I was not able to! I have tried to go back as far as `opencode upgrade 1.3.0`! Then did uninstall and install via `npm uninstall -g opencode-ai@latest` and `npm i -g opencode-ai@latest` and just settled for this script as a workaround...


